<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 39.8 percent of their 1996/97 sunflower crop by March 3, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Friday.</p>
<p>Attacks by Rio Cuarto virus on maize crops should mean production is about 14.35 million tonnes, two percent lower than estimates a month ago. Rio Cuarto has cost about 384,000 tonnes in lost production. Maize harvesting was 14.6 percent complete. First crop soybeans are generall evolving well thorughout the country, except in Cordoba and in central Santa Fe, where there are problems of dryness.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,814  100.0(100.0)   505.1   14.6   (5.3)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,412  100.0(100.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,039  100.0(100.0)   905.2   39.8  (38.9)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770  100.0(100.0)    22.7    3.0   (0.1)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	953  100.0  (n/a)     6.6    0.8   (1.6)    (n/a)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655))</p>
